  "description": "VEBZEJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C130 H95 Er5 O25 S10,0.5(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.510-5.026 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.72-158.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C130H95Er5O25S10·0.5(C7H8). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
